e list and branch -D; rejected: pre-existing shape and git itself refuses -D on a checked-out branch\" disposition=rejected","description":"Record finding 9"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Df15T2D1WYNipktFJzjFMB","tool_input":{"command":"../flywheel/guard.sh finding lens=security file=tools/fleet/run.go line=569 severity=low claim=\"deleting a tree-equal branch loses its commit messages; rejected: content is on main by construction and this is the same deletion the previous code made\" disposition=rejected","description":"Record finding 10"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qn74KW1gwtSg1yGdRSCvsv","tool_input":{"command":"../flywheel/guard.sh finding lens=security file=tools/fleet/run.go line=564 severity=low claim=\"base is HEAD not refs/heads/main; rejected: base is by design the commit the worktree is cut from (run.go:232) and changing that is outside this bead\" disposition=rejected","description":"Record finding 11"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GgJsAh9LrX1EaFAuidZKbh","tool_input":{"command":"../flywheel/guard.sh finding lens=simplicity file=tools/fleet/emptybranch_test.go line=66 severity=medium claim=\"four scenario tests could be one table; rejected: the file is narrative per-function tests and each case asserts something different (commitsSince setup check, distinct substrings); mixing styles costs more than the duplication\" disposition=rejected","description":"Record finding 12"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MUViezusanxhYtHRU2b8bh","tool_input":{"command":"../flywheel/guard.sh finding lens=simplicity file=tools/fleet/run.go line=577 severity=low claim=\"message hard-coded against main while base is a parameter; folded into finding 2, message now names base\" disposition=accepted","description":"Record finding 13"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DZ2dqfKHJbtHhS4kfByffd","tool_input":{"command":"git clean -f -- tools/fleet/fleet","description":"Remove the untracked fleet binary go build produced"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":3,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":3,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"general-purpose":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":112,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"## Report — fw-web\n\n**Bead taken:** fw-web (P2 bug) — a stale pre-rewrite branch reads as 23 commits of work and can never be swept. Ran **solo** (`run-context.json: solo=true`), so no blackbird registration or reservation.\n\n**What I did:** `clearEmptyBranch` (`tools/fleet/run.go:552`) now judges a leftover branch by **tree**, not commit count. A branch is cleared iff its tree equals the merge-base's tree or any tree on `mb..base`. One deliberate deviation from the bead's design note, stated in the PR: comparing against the merge-base *alone* doesn't fix the real fw-ax2 case, because after a rewrite the merge-base sits behind the rewritten range — the stale tree matches its rewritten twin on main, not the merge-base. The window starts at the merge-base on purpose so a branch that deleted something main kept is still refused. Refusals name the file count against main; everything git can't answer (no merge-base, empty base, unlistable worktrees) fails closed. Six new/rewritten tests cover both halves of the acceptance criteria plus the refusals.\n\n**Gate:** green — lefthook pre-commit (gofmt, vet, vet-conformance, short tests, identity, replay-guard) on all three commits; push-guard on push.\n\n**Review (ADR 0013):** three-lens panel, 13 findings → `.flywheel/review.jsonl` (45 → 58 lines). 7 accepted and applied (file count was against the merge-base, \"0 file(s) changed\" self-contradiction — flagged by two lenses — fail-open worktree check, misleading empty-base message, `revParse` rename, helper migration, root-commit comment). 6 rejected with reasons in the ledger.\n\n**PR:** https://github.com/jamesponwith/agentic-flywheel/pull/70 — weight `w:2`, bead left open, not merged.\n\n**Not done / notes:**\n- A stray `tools/fleet/fleet` binary from `go build` sits untracked in the worktree; both `rm` and `git clean` were blocked by the sandbox. It's untracked and not in any commit — harmless, but worth a `git clean` when you remove the worktree.\n- Worktree left in place for the spawner to remove.\n- Cost not measured in-session (the spawner records `bead.cost`).","ttft_ms":3644,"type":"result","duration_ms":553747,"uuid":"c3812e5c-4b64-46c7-b704-b520e6b3f5a5","ttft_stream_ms":2848,"time_to_request_ms":108,"queued_turn_count":0}
